      "message": "Nope, that\u0027s my main concern (the BUILD_TYPEs have been effectively obsolete forever). Colin\u0027s comment about preserving PRODUCT_SOONG_CONFIGs somewhere is also a good idea, but I definitely agree it\u0027s gotten spammy in the main banner.\n\nAs for other variables that may not be as useful anymore:\n\nHOST_ARCH/HOST_2ND_ARCH/HOST_CROSS_ARCH/HOST_CROSS_2ND_ARCH may not be useful, not sure. My impression is that they should be pretty static these days based on HOST_OS.\n\nI think AUX_OS_VARIANT_LIST is obsolete (though that means it shouldn\u0027t be printed)",
